{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>A Hebrew man, of his brethren.</b> The precision of saying <b>of his brethren</b> alludes to the fact that he looked upon him as one of the righteous among Israel, for at that time there were wicked men in Israel. Go out and learn from what they said, of blessed memory (Mekhilta on Exodus 12:29), concerning the verse ״וַחֲמֻשִׁים עָלוּ״ etc. (Exodus 13:18) — that four parts [of Israel perished]; and according to the one who says more, they died during the days of darkness, while the rest went up, on account of their being wicked. <b>And you will find</b> that when Scripture says shortly after, ״שְׁנֵי אֲנָשִׁים עִבְרִים נִצִּים״, it does not say ״of his brethren,״ for the reason that they were wicked — for they were Dathan and Abiram (Exodus Rabbah 1:29)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:32.009854682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}